diff --git a/NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md b/NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md
index dd1e60e..c5a39ba 100644
--- a/NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md
+++ b/NETIE-ATTRIBUTION.md
@@ -1,7 +1,7 @@
 # Attribution
 
 Netie FreeIDE for VS Code is a modified distribution of Kilo-Org/kilocode
-(https://github.com/Kilo-Org/kilocode), pinned at commit 831805118a.
+(https://github.com/Kilo-Org/kilocode), pinned at commit a93088bfe2.
 
 Upstream license: MIT. LICENSE is included unmodified, with every
 upstream copyright line, and so is any NOTICE file.
@@ -23,3 +23,63 @@ logos belong to their owners.
 - SECURITY, SUPPORT and CONTRIBUTING contacts and URLs still point at upstream.
 - Translated docs, changelogs and third-party notices are untouched.
 - Netie gate wiring: Same as freeide. Both copyright lines (Kilo Code, opencode) stay in LICENSE.
+
+## Stage 2 gate patch (written, not run yet)
+
+Written by hand on top of stage 1, in `packages/kilo-vscode` plus this file. Nothing in it
+has been compiled, tested, bundled or replayed yet, so stage 2 is not done: the list above
+still holds for everything this patch does not change.
+
+- New sessions default to `openvault/auto`: the `kilo-code.new.model.*` setting defaults
+  and the fallback `NETIE_DEFAULT` in `src/shared/provider-model.ts`. A model set in the
+  user's own config still wins.
+- The backend the extension starts gets `NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL` (default
+  `http://127.0.0.1:5000`), `KILO_PURE=false` and `KILO_CONFIG_CONTENT` from
+  `src/netie/openvault.ts`. That config adds provider `openvault` (OpenVault FreeRoute at
+  `NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL` + `/v1`, `@ai-sdk/openai-compatible`, no key sent) and the gate
+  plugin. `KILO_PURE` is always overridden because with it set the backend loads no
+  external plugin, the gate included.
+- A `KILO_CONFIG_CONTENT` the user set is not merged. The backend drops all of that
+  variable, gate included, when any part of it fails to load (`{file:}` or `{env:}`
+  substitution, JSON, schema) and only records a warning. So the backend does not start
+  while one is set, and the error says to move that config into kilo.json.
+- Gate plugin `dist/netie-openvault-gate.js`, bundled from
+  `src/netie/openvault-gate-plugin.ts`, hooks `tool.execute.before` on the session tool
+  path the extension uses and POSTs `/api/crew/gate` to OpenVault before every tool except
+  a short local list: `read`, `glob`, `grep`, `todowrite`, `question`, `task`, `invalid`.
+  That exemption holds only while the backend's tool registry lists the id once, so a
+  plugin or config-dir tool that takes one of these ids is gated. MCP tools, plugin tools,
+  `bash`, `edit`, `write`, `apply_patch`, `webfetch`, `websearch`, `skill` and `lsp` are
+  all gated. The body is ids only (kind, id, intent, parent_run_id, child_id, deficit),
+  never tool arguments. Unreachable, non-JSON, a non-2xx reply, or anything but
+  `allowed: true` stops the tool with an error. There is no offline mode, and no setting
+  or env flag turns the gate off.
+- The backend does not start when the gate bundle is missing, and the error names the
+  file. A plugin the backend cannot load is only reported, and tools would run ungated.
+- Inline autocomplete no longer triggers by default: its only default route is the Kilo
+  account, a vendor route outside OpenVault.
+- Extension display name, activity bar title, sidebar view name and command category read
+  FreeIDE for VS Code.
+- Proof to run: `packages/kilo-vscode/tests/unit/netie-openvault-gate.test.ts`. The end to
+  end case (real backend, fake OpenVault, a refused `bash` call) is not written yet, so
+  that the backend skips a tool whose hook throws is read from code, not measured.
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+- Package name `kilo-code`, publisher `kilocode`, the `kilo-code.new.*` command ids and
+  setting keys (renaming them needs a settings migration), and the logo.
+- Other UI strings still say Kilo Code: code actions, OS notifications, the settings
+  title, the editor and terminal context submenus, and webview text.
+- The anonymous `kilo` provider autoload in the core
+  (`packages/opencode/src/kilocode/provider/provider.ts`) is still on.
+- Autocomplete is not routed through OpenVault; that needs a FIM endpoint OpenVault does
+  not document.
+- Subscription-login providers are not switched off (DR-0002 rule 6).
+- The same backend also serves the V2 session API, whose runner runs core tools (`bash`,
+  `edit`, `write`, `webfetch` and others) with no plugin hook, so the gate does not cover
+  it. The extension does not call that API today, and the gate test fails if `src` or
+  `webview-ui` starts to.
+- With `lsp` enabled in the user's config, an ungated `read` can start language servers
+  and download them from npm or GitHub without asking OpenVault.
+- No vsix has been built and installed in VS Code with the gate refusing a real `bash`
+  call against a real OpenVault.
